      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structsl__bt__evt__system__resource__exhausted__s_1a97dd311e4778d68e48a1a82bdb816499" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>uint8_t</type>
        <definition>uint8_t sl_bt_evt_system_resource_exhausted_s::num_buffers_discarded</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>num_buffers_discarded</name>
        <qualifiedname>sl_bt_evt_system_resource_exhausted_s::num_buffers_discarded</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The system has temporarily run out of the pre-allocated data buffers that are allocated based on SL_BT_CONFIG_BUFFER_SIZE configuration and some expendable data or event had to be discarded to satisfy a non-expendble buffer allocation. A typical case is discarding scan reports when a large inflow of scan reports exceeds the speed at which the application drains the BGAPI event queue. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
